Find resources in the installed prefix, relative to the library

KB_LAYOUT_DIR, COLORSCHEMES_DIR and TRANSLATIONS_DIR are baked into the library
as absolute paths from CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR. Under MSYS2 the install
prefix is a POSIX path, so what lands in the DLL is

    /ucrt64/share/qtermwidget6/color-schemes

which a native Windows binary resolves against the current drive root -- it
never exists. The failure is silent and total: availableColorSchemes() and
availableKeyBindings() return empty lists and no translation is ever loaded.

Patch 0001 already added a Windows fallback for all three, but it looks beside
the *executable* -- applicationDirPath()/kb-layouts/ and friends. That is the
right shape for a self-contained application directory, where a bundler has
copied the resources next to the .exe. It is the wrong shape for a package
manager, which installs them once into

    $PREFIX/share/qtermwidget6/...

and leaves the DLL in $PREFIX/bin. So this adds a second fallback, tried after
0001's, that resolves relative to the module rather than the application:
CMake computes the data directory relative to BINDIR and passes it as
QTERMWIDGET_DATA_RELDIR, and get_module_dir() asks the loader for this DLL's
own path via GetModuleHandleEx(FROM_ADDRESS).

The module and not applicationDirPath() on purpose. kb-layouts and
color-schemes belong to the library, and a consumer executable is under no
obligation to sit in the same directory as the DLL -- during this package's own
smoke test it did not, which is exactly how the empty lists were noticed.

Ordering is deliberate: the compiled-in absolute path first, then 0001's
app-directory lookup, then this one. A bundler who has deliberately placed
resources next to the executable still wins; the prefix layout is the fallback
for everyone who has not.

Kept separate from 0001 rather than folded into it so that refreshing the
vendored PR stays a clean drop-in. See 0001's header for that PR's status.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments (the new code is behind Q_OS_WIN)

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -221,8 +221,20 @@
     set_target_properties(${QTERMWIDGET_LIBRARY_NAME} PROPERTIES INSTALL_NAME_DIR ${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDIR})
 endif()
 
+# Windows installs have no fixed filesystem prefix -- the tree is unpacked
+# wherever the user puts it, and under MSYS2 the configure-time prefix is a
+# POSIX path that a native binary cannot resolve at all. Record the data
+# directory relative to bin/ as well, so the library can locate its resources
+# next to itself at runtime. Relative to bin/ rather than to the prefix because
+# that is where the DLL lands, and the DLL is what does the lookup.
+file(RELATIVE_PATH QTERMWIDGET_DATA_RELDIR
+    "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/${CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR}"
+    "${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR}/${QTERMWIDGET_LIBRARY_NAME}"
+)
+
 target_compile_definitions(${QTERMWIDGET_LIBRARY_NAME}
     PRIVATE
+        "QTERMWIDGET_DATA_RELDIR=\"${QTERMWIDGET_DATA_RELDIR}\""
         "KB_LAYOUT_DIR=\"${KB_LAYOUT_DIR}\""
         "COLORSCHEMES_DIR=\"${COLORSCHEMES_DIR}\""
         "TRANSLATIONS_DIR=\"${TRANSLATIONS_DIR}\""
